        "original_id": "cc2a9ef7-42bb-54d3-95b6-ea65fb746fe3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rob Bottin, David Fincher, John Carpenter, Paul Verhoeven\n- Roles: special make-up effects creator, director, producer\n- Works: The Fog, The Thing, RoboCop, Total Recall, Basic Instinct, Se7en, Fight Club, The Curious Case of Benjamin Button, The Social Network\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Director, Golden Globe Award for Best Director, BAFTA Award for Best Direction\n\nFacts:\n- Rob Bottin, born April 1, 1959, is an American special make-up effects creator.\n- David Fincher, born August 28, 1962, is an American director and producer known for films, television series, and music videos.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with John Carpenter on The Fog and The Thing.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with Paul Verhoeven on RoboCop, Total Recall, and Basic Instinct.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with David Fincher on Se7en and Fight Club.\n- David Fincher was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director for The Curious Case of Benjamin Button in 2008.\n- David Fincher was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director for The Social Network in 2010.\n- David Fincher won the Golden Globe Award for Best Director and the BAFTA Award for Best Direction for The Social Network.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
